<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	<style>/* Noto Sans Malayalam loads via a <link rel="stylesheet"> in <head> now (podcast.astro, slot
   "head" — added to Base.astro for this), not an @import in this inlined <style>: an @import
   here was render-blocking the whole stylesheet behind a second font fetch and showed up as a
   real mobile LCP regression (hero text became the LCP element at ~4.5s instead of the hero
   image at well under 2s) — fixed by moving it to <head> where the browser discovers it during
   initial HTML parse, same as every other font link on this site. */

/* One accent-text colour this page needs that tokens.css doesn't have a light-mode-safe version
   of: --teal-hi (#8fa838 in light mode) is calibrated for icons/large marks elsewhere, not body
   text — on white it's 2.68:1, under both the 3:1 (large) and 4.5:1 (normal) WCAG AA minimums.
   --pc-accent-text is a darkened lime that clears 4.5:1 (4.88:1), for the two places this page
   puts the accent in actual text (the hero's emphasised span, the episode-card tag labels). */
:root { --pc-accent-text: #507c41; }

/* WiseUp Podcast (/podcast), rebuilt on the homepage's own design system (2026-10-23): same
   Base/Header/Footer, same tokens.css palette (teal/lime accent, Epilogue + Inter), same card/
   button/eyebrow/FAQ/hgal/loop classes from site.css, forced to the light ("day") mood throughout
   rather than the site's usual dark default. Only truly podcast-specific shapes get new rules
   here (`.pc-*`), scoped and inlined the same way about.css is. Noto Sans Malayalam is the one
   addition with no homepage equivalent: Epilogue/Inter don't carry Malayalam glyphs, and this
   page has real Malayalam headline/quote text to render. */

.pc-ml { font-family: 'Noto Sans Malayalam', 'Inter', sans-serif; }

/* Tighter section rhythm than the homepage's own .sec (padding-block: calc(var(--sec) * 0.6),
   ~58-108px) — scoped to this page's own wrapper so the homepage/About/Contact keep their normal
   spacing. This page has many more, shorter sections back to back (episodes/topics/people/faq/
   guest) than a typical homepage section, so the usual rhythm reads as too much dead air between
   them. */
.pc-page .sec { padding-block: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 64px); }
/* .pc-page .sec (two classes) is more specific than .pc-hero alone (one), so without this it was
   overriding the hero's own padding-top — stripping its clearance for the fixed header and
   letting the header overlap the hero content. Restore it at equal specificity to the rule above. */
.pc-page .sec.pc-hero { padding-top: calc(var(--head-h) + clamp(28px, 5vh, 64px)); }

/* ---- hero ---- */
.pc-hero { padding-top: calc(var(--head-h) + clamp(32px, 6vh, 80px)); padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); }
